Do not take zutil.h's Classic Mac OS branch on modern Apple systems.

TARGET_OS_MAC is 1 in the iOS SDK (it is Apple's umbrella target macro,
not "macOS only"), and the Classic-Mac branch this header selects then
does `#define fdopen(fd,mode) NULL`. That collides with the SDK's real
`fdopen` prototype and every translation unit that includes <stdio.h>
after zlib fails to compile. Modern Apple platforms carry the fdopen
call in their libc and pick up the correct OS_CODE=19 from the __APPLE__
branch below, so this whole block is only there for the true Classic
Mac OS toolchain — exclude __APPLE__ from it.

diff --git a/zutil.h b/zutil.h
--- a/zutil.h
+++ b/zutil.h
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@
 #  define OS_CODE 0
 #endif

-#if defined(MACOS) || defined(TARGET_OS_MAC)
+#if (defined(MACOS) || defined(TARGET_OS_MAC)) && !defined(__APPLE__)
 #  define OS_CODE  7
 #  ifndef Z_SOLO
 #    if defined(__MWERKS__) && __dest_os != __be_os && __dest_os != __win32_os
